   454→   454→+// TestPostCommit_Issue591_SubagentScaleRegression is a regression test for GitHub
   455→   455→+// issue #591. It creates exactly 76 ENDED sessions (the reported accumulation count)
   456→   456→+// whose files don't overlap with a later commit, then verifies:
   457→   457→+//
   458→   458→+//  1. First PostCommit force-condenses all 76 zombie sessions and marks them FullyCondensed.
   459→   459→+//  2. Second PostCommit (the commit that was taking 2m44s before the fix) completes
   460→   460→+//     well under 2 seconds — all sessions are skipped via the FullyCondensed fast-path.
   461→   461→+//
   462→   462→+// Before fix: ~73-103ms × 76 sessions = ~5.5–8s per commit, forever.
   463→   463→+// After fix: one-time force-condense cost on first PostCommit, then ~O(1) per commit.
